Third-party work
----------------
The inference notebooks in pipeline/ embed and run code from public Kaggle notebooks and datasets. That code
keeps its original license and attribution:

* nartaa: Raptor CoAtNet inference notebooks ("RSNA Knee 0949 Anatomical Mirror", "RSNA Knee 0945 Efficient
  224crop"), SWA checkpoints (dataset rsna-knee-publication-swa-weights-20261007) and the S6 all-data model
  (dataset rsna-knee-s6fall-weights).
* dreaddevelopment: Raptor CoAtNet/MIL inference recipe and public baseline weights
  (https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/dreaddevelopment/raptor-knee-widedense).
* heliosli: R6 compact ConvNeXt bundle (dataset rsna-knee-r6-frozen-fe055406-w1) and OrthoFoundation code
  (dataset rsna-orthofoundation-fold0-epoch7-20261004).
* goodpjw2008: 2.5D ConvNeXt MIL reader (Apache 2.0, dataset rsna-knee-2-5d-convnext-reader) and the public
  "CoAtNet + R6 + 2.5D MIL" recipe that the v74 notebook forks.
* varshithakolupuri: the 224-pixel stage and its 35 % share of the Raptor half
  (https://www.kaggle.com/code/varshithakolupuri/rsna-knee-one-unused-checkpoint-lifts-the-0-956).
* Weak-label sources used by the Raptor checkpoints: stevenleehans (rsna-knee-llm-report-labels),
  pilkwang (rsna-knee-llm-labels), riadmohamed42 (JEV labels and verification).
* The CoAtNet and ConvNeXt backbones come from timm.

